Rice being offered during a rare and sacred ritual to make peace with nature and the spirits believed to reside around the Sindang Gili waterfall located on the slopes of Mount Rinjani on the Indonesian island of Lombok. The water, which originates from the sacred volcano, is considered the holiest water from the active volcano. The water is often collected by the Wetu Telu and Sasak people of Lombok and considered sacred by the Balinese who often make a religious pilgrimage to this volcanic island. It is believe that after the ritual is completed, the power of the waterfall increases and changes is position from hitting the first rock to moving and hitting the second rock.

